From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: retroforge <retroforge@invalid>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(InputManager): don't ask DBus whether InputPlumber runs
 on every input event

InputManager._input() runs for every input event and asked
InputPlumberInstance.is_running() each time, which builds a DBus proxy
and makes a blocking NameHasOwner round trip. During a game Godot's
joypad driver reads InputPlumber's virtual gamepad, so every stick and
button change cost a round trip and was then dropped: on a MANGMI Air X
~194 NameHasOwner calls a second from OGUI while playing, about 1 ms of
OGUI CPU per gamepad event (main thread and the zbus threads) and
~20 ms/s in dbus-broker (2026-11-22, Megabonk).

InputPlumberRunning (core/systems/input/input_plumber_running.gd) asks
at most once a second and takes the instance's started / stopped
signals at once. InputManager and OverlayInputManager drop a joypad
event first thing, before building its debug message;
is_action_pressed() and the D-Pad double-input check use the same
answer.

---
  core/systems/input/input_manager.gd              | 23 +++++++-----
  core/systems/input/input_plumber_running.gd      | 48 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
  core/systems/input/overlay_mode_input_manager.gd | 14 ++++---
  3 files changed, 70 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

